{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>When your son asks you tomorrow.</b> 'Tomorrow' means after some time." "<b>Which HaShem our Elohim commanded you.</b> The verse speaks of a wise son, who investigates so carefully into the reason for the commandments. And in that he said <b>'you'</b> — he did not exclude himself from the collective, for since he said <b>'HaShem our Elohim'</b> he accepted upon himself the yoke of the kingdom of heaven. And the <b>'you'</b> he mentions is only because he was not born at the time of the command. But one who says, 'What is this service to you?' and does not mention the Name of heaven — excludes himself from the collective of the service, for it implies it does not apply to him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:00.065506595Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}